---
import ResourceLayout from '../../components/ResourceLayout.astro';
---

<ResourceLayout
  icon="👶"
  eyebrow="Pregnancy, children, and prevention"
  title="Family Health"
  introduction="Learn about pregnancy care, children’s healthcare, vaccinations, routine checkups, and preventive screening in Canada."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Pregnancy care</h2>
    <p>
      Pregnancy care may be provided by a family doctor, midwife, obstetrician,
      or nurse practitioner. Regular appointments help monitor the health of the
      pregnant person and the developing baby.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Healthcare for babies and children</h2>
    <p>
      Babies and children should have regular checkups to monitor growth,
      development, nutrition, hearing, vision, and overall health. These visits
      are also a good time to ask questions about sleep, feeding, and behaviour.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Vaccinations</h2>
    <p>
      Routine vaccines help protect children and adults from serious infectious
      diseases. Provincial and territorial vaccination schedules may differ, so
      ask a healthcare provider or public health clinic which vaccines are
      recommended.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>School and public health services</h2>
    <p>
      Some vaccinations, dental programs, hearing tests, and other health
      services may be offered through schools or local public health units.
      Availability depends on the province, territory, and community.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Screening and prevention</h2>
    <p>
      Preventive care may include blood pressure checks, cancer screening,
      prenatal testing, developmental screening, and other tests based on age,
      health history, and individual risk.
    </p>
  </section>

  <aside class="notice">
    <strong>When a child needs urgent help</strong>
    <p>
      Call 911 or seek emergency care if a child has severe difficulty
      breathing, is difficult to wake, has a seizure, develops blue lips, has
      major bleeding, or appears seriously unwell.
    </p>
  </aside>
</ResourceLayout>